  "statement": "\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn the figure, the sphere fits perfectly in the cube; that is, it touches each face exactly in the center point of the face.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAssume the sphere has radius \u003ci\u003er\u003c/i\u003e.\u003ci\u003e \u003c/i\u003eUse your calculator to find the volume of the region inside the cube but outside the sphere for different values of \u003ci\u003er\u003c/i\u003e. What is the least whole–number value of \u003ci\u003er\u003c/i\u003e for which the volume of this region is greater than 100 cubic units?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class\u003d\"problemstatement_figure\"\u003e\n \u003cimg src\u003d\"/modules/gcprealgpractice/gcprealgpractice_9_1_areasandvolumes_2_80/f-80-2-q.gif\"\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e",
  "statementFigure": null,
  "question": null,
  "widgetSlot": null,
  "steps": [
    {
      "role": "hint",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eFind the volume of the cube.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
    {
      "role": "step",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eThe cube has side length 2\u003ci\u003er\u003c/i\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eThe volume of a cube with side length \u003ci\u003es\u003c/i\u003e units is \u003ci\u003es\u003c/i\u003e\u003csup\u003e3\u003c/sup\u003e square units.\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eSo, the cube has volume (2\u003ci\u003er\u003c/i\u003e)\u003csup\u003e3\u003c/sup\u003e \u003d 8\u003ci\u003er\u003c/i\u003e\u003csup\u003e3\u003c/sup\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\u003cimg class\u003d\"graphimgstatic id\u003d\" figure-1 src\u003d\"/modules/gcprealgpractice/gcprealgpractice_9_1_areasandvolumes_2_80/f-80-2-q.gif\"\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
    {
      "role": "hint",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eFind the volume of the sphere.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
    {
      "role": "step",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eThe volume of the sphere is simply\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003e\u003cimg width\u003d\"44\" height\u003d\"41\" src\u003d\"/modules/gcprealgpractice/gcprealgpractice_9_1_areasandvolumes_2_80/image001.gif\" class\u003d\"middle\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
    {
      "role": "hint",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eFind the area of the region inside the cube but outside the sphere.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
    {
      "role": "step",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eSubtract to find the area of the region inside the cube but outside the sphere.\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003e\u003cimg width\u003d\"104\" height\u003d\"41\" src\u003d\"/modules/gcprealgpractice/gcprealgpractice_9_1_areasandvolumes_2_80/image002.gif\" class\u003d\"middle\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
    {
      "role": "hint",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eEnter this function in your calculator.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
